<title>USA: Prime Retail revises full-yr loss to $0.75.</title>
<headline>Prime Retail revises full-yr loss to $0.75.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Retail Inc said it restated its full-year loss, released Tuesday, to $0.75 from $1.15 per share, due to the reallocation of a second-quarter extraordinary loss.</p>
<p>The company's fourth-quarter results are unchanged.</p>
<p>The restated results are as follow:</p>
<p>					 Three Months Ended  Year Ended</p>
<p>						December 31  December 31</p>
<p>					  1996    1995    1996     1995</p>
<p>    Total revenues		25,928  21,329  89,040   77,398</p>
<p> Net income			  1,136   4,582   8,061   18,170</p>
<p>   Net loss			 (0.14)  (0.23)  (0.75)   (0.96)</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>  common shares outstanding   13,405   2,875   8,221    2,875</p>
<p>(Amounts in thousands, except per share results.)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 year results include a $10.4 million one-time loss on debt refinancing. On Tuesday, part of the loss was overstated to common shareholders, the company said.</p>
</text>
